 @robertg457  The main concern when buying used tech for me is how well they will age.

And considering that the GTX 1070 and the base design of this RX590, the RX480, launched very close to each other they don't give each other much in that regard. 

AFAIK Polaris does support a few more features of the DX12 standard that offer performance improvements, but these should've been well used by now so current benchmarks should already include any potential gains that brings.

 @jowarnis  I don't get this card. It's out a year too late.
I'd not be happy using one a year down the line, never mind two.
It's not a bad card but if it was out in 2016 like the 1060 you'd have got some good value from it.

@Jose Sagredo
Nope, it's twice the cost(today) and about 10-15% better performance. (probably from auto oc)

In case you forgot; 970 also compares with 980.   1060 does not compare with 980ti, 980ti compares with 1070, while there is a pretty big gap between 1060 and 1070.
